<p>The <b>Trilateral Cooperation Secretariat</b> (<b>TCS</b>) is an <a href="/wiki/Intergovernmental_organization" class="mw-redirect" title="Intergovernmental organization">international organization</a> established with a vision to promote "Lasting Peace, Common Prosperity, and Shared Culture" among <a href="/wiki/China" title="China">China</a>, <a href="/wiki/Japan" title="Japan">Japan</a>, and <a href="/wiki/South_Korea" title="South Korea">South Korea</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-2" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-2"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>2<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup> Upon the agreement signed and ratified by each of the three governments, the TCS was officially inaugurated in <a href="/wiki/Seoul" title="Seoul">Seoul</a>, on 1 September 2011.<sup id="cite_ref-3" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-3"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>3<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup> On the basis of equal participation, each government shares 1/3 of the total operational budget.
</p>
